  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["J11", "Q1"],
      "pins": ["J11.15", "J11.16", "Q1.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0016 (Display_Power_Switch)"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet the FPC connector J11 (FH34SRJ-24S-0.5SH(99)) carries no-connect (X) markers on pins 15 and 16, and the Display_Power_Switch net (NET0016, the drain of the high-side load switch Q1/NTR2101P) is wired only to the boost-converter input side (L2, C4, C11). No wire or label connects NET0016 to J11.15/J11.16.",
      "expected": "Per the specification, the Q2/Q1 drain (Display_Power_Switch) must feed J1.15/J1.16 (the panel's VDDIO/VDD pins) in addition to the boost converter's L1/C1/C2, so the switched 3.3 V reaches the e-paper panel's logic/display supply.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Q2.3 (drain) ties to the Display_Power_Switch net, which feeds J1.15/J1.16 — the EPD panel's VDDIO/VDD pins per the PDI pin table — plus the EPD boost converter's L1, C1, C2. (EPD_Driver section)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch: J11 pins 15 and 16 shown with no-connect 'X' markers; NET0016 label connects only to L2/C4/C11 (boost input), not to the connector."}
      ],
      "impact": "The e-paper panel's VDD/VDDIO supply is never energized even when the power-switch MOSFET turns on, so the panel cannot respond to SPI commands or refresh; the display is effectively dead.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All component identities and values match the specification, but on the EPD_Driver sheet the Display_Power_Switch rail (NET0016) is connected only to the boost-converter input and the connector's VDD/VDDIO pins (J11.15/16) are left as no-connect, contradicting the spec's stated wiring that this net feeds J1.15/J1.16 — leaving the e-paper panel unpowered."
}

